[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     24[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Rust translation of `src/mdmacros.h`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     25[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     26[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! The C header does all of its work in the preprocessor: token pasting picks
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     27[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! an `op_<OP>` function, a `STEP_<OP>` expression, an `INIT_<OP>` seed, and a
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     28[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `REP<REPEAT>` manual unrolling. None of that survives into the object file,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     29[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! so the Rust equivalent resolves the same choices at compile time with
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     30[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! `#[cfg(feature = ...)]` and `const`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     31[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //!
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     32[0m:[38;5;10m[49m //! Feature -> CMake mapping:
