[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     4[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     5[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// `int atoi(const char *nptr)`.
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     6[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ///
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     7[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// glibc implements this as `(int) strtol(nptr, NULL, 10)`: leading whitespace is
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     8[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// skipped, an optional sign is consumed, digits are accumulated until the first
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+     9[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// non-digit, and a string with no digits at all yields 0. Out-of-range input
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    10[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// saturates at `LONG_MAX`/`LONG_MIN` inside `strtol` and is then truncated by the
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    11[0m:[38;5;10m[49m /// cast to `int`, which is what the `i64` saturation plus `as c_int` below
